@page "/"
@using System.Globalization
@inject DailySchedule Schedule

<PageTitle>Stumpty — Challenge of the day</PageTitle>

<div class="oad-home">
    @* Today's date, not the teaser's. The distinction matters: with the recycling
       box the teaser on screen may have been written months ago, so printing its
       own date would give away that the puzzle is a repeat. AppTime.Today is the
       Pacific clock the whole schedule runs on, so this always agrees with the
       countdown and with which challenge is live. *@
    <p class="oad-dateline">@AppTime.Today.ToString("dddd, MMMM d", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</p>

    <div class="oad-banner">Challenge of the day</div>

    @if (_teaser is null)
    {
        <div class="oad-box">
            <h2>Question:</h2>
            <p>No brain teaser has been posted yet. Check back soon!</p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @* No date note any more: with the recycling box there is always a challenge
           for today, and saying "from 3 July" would both read as an apology and give
           away that the puzzle is a repeat. The Challenge of the day never reveals
           its own answer either — that surfaces on /yesterday tomorrow. *@
        <ChallengeView Teaser="_teaser" IsDaily="true" CanReveal="false" />
    }
</div>

@* Deliberately only on the Challenge of the day page. *@
<ReportIssue />

@code {
    private BrainTeaser? _teaser;
    private DateOnly _today;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _today = AppTime.Today;
        _teaser = Schedule.ForDay(_today);
    }
}
